{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: H06 — Approval workflow: transition + associated-data invariant\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: State-machine invariant (2/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic approval-workflow program\n(single module). A case has a status from `Draft / UnderReview / Approved /\nRejected` and already carries a `decision_reason` string field (no schema\nevolution needed). Operations: `submit`, `approve`, `reject(reason)`,\n`reopen`. The current rules are **looser** than the required contract (e.g.,\na draft can be approved directly, an empty reject reason is accepted, and a\nstale decision reason survives approve/reopen). There is no persistence, no\nwall-clock dependency, and no restart logic.\n\nThe program is driven by the environment variable `H06_SCENARIO` and prints\ndeterministic lines.\n\n## Required change\n\nTighten the workflow to exactly:\n\n```text\nsubmit:        Draft       -> UnderReview\napprove:       UnderReview -> Approved      (decision_reason MUST be cleared)\nreject(reason): UnderReview -> Rejected     (reason MUST be non-empty and saved)\nreopen:        Rejected    -> UnderReview   (decision_reason MUST be cleared)\n```\n\nwith the invariants:\n\n- `Approved` may not be reopened or rejected;\n- `Draft` may not be approved or rejected;\n- a `Rejected` case may not be rejected again;\n- any illegal transition must fail with an explicit error whose text starts\n  with `E_H06_STATE:` and names the operation and the source state;\n- rejecting with an empty reason must fail with an explicit error whose text\n  starts with `E_H06_REASON:`;\n- every transition must preserve all other case data (notably `note`).\n\nDo not add fields, do not add states, do not touch persistence or restart.\nExisting legal behavior must be preserved exactly.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier drives the compiled program through scenarios and checks\nexact output lines: the legal paths, the full illegal-transition matrix, the\n`decision_reason` invariants (cleared on approve/reopen, non-empty on reject,\nstale reasons removed), and preservation of unrelated fields.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; the verifier is\nnot visible to you.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
